{
  "id": "u13-l04",
  "unit": "u13-requests",
  "title": "Could you…? Thanks!",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**A command is fine for offers** (বসুন, চা নিন). **To ask a favour, a question is softer** (U12): **আপনি কি দরজা খুলতে পারবেন?** 'Could you open the door?' To a friend: **তুমি কি … পারবে?**\n\n**প্লিজ**, from English, is everywhere in Bangladeshi speech and sounds more casual than **দয়া করে**: **প্লিজ, দরজা বন্ধ করো** 'Close the door, please'.\n\n**Thanks:** **অনেক ধন্যবাদ** 'Thank you very much'. Replies: **কোনো ব্যাপার না** 'It's nothing' or **কোনো সমস্যা নেই** 'No problem'.\n\n*Culture:* with family and close friends, ধন্যবাদ can sound stiff; people often just smile and say **আচ্ছা**.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "plij",
      "bn": "প্লিজ",
      "tr": "plij",
      "en": "please",
      "notes": "From English. Very common in Bangladeshi speech, more casual than দয়া করে."
    },
    {
      "id": "khulte",
      "bn": "খুলতে",
      "tr": "khulte",
      "en": "to open",
      "notes": "Infinitive of খোলা 'open': খুলি → খুল- + -তে (the vowel rises, as in শুনতে)."
    },
    {
      "id": "dekhate",
      "bn": "দেখাতে",
      "tr": "dekhate",
      "en": "to show",
      "notes": "Infinitive of দেখানো 'show' (from দেখা 'see')."
    },
    {
      "id": "dorja",
      "bn": "দরজা",
      "tr": "dorja",
      "en": "door"
    },
    {
      "id": "byapar",
      "bn": "ব্যাপার",
      "tr": "byapar",
      "en": "matter; thing",
      "notes": "কোনো ব্যাপার না 'no problem, it's nothing': a common reply to thanks."
    }
  ],
